-- Migration: Import real employee/asset/software roster data uploaded by the user
-- (PPS EC(PTech) hardware & software allocation sheet: 296 sheet rows covering 203
-- distinct employees, 12 shared/placeholder computers (Free/Conference/Tekla/etc),
-- 75 unassigned spare computers, and 245 software allocation line items). Seeds
-- entities, clients, software catalog, users, hardware assets, and per-line
-- license_inventory/license_allocations so the app reflects the organization's
-- actual current-state data instead of being empty.
--
-- Data notes:
-- * Shared/placeholder computers (Free/Conference/Tekla/User-nnn) and fully unassigned
--   spare computers get an assets row with NULL assigned_user_id, no users row.
-- * department_id defaults to the existing PTECH department for all imported rows since
--   the source sheet has no org-department breakdown distinct from entity.
-- * license_inventory models one row per software-allocation line item (total_seats=1)
--   to preserve each line's own purchase cost / expiry date / client context, rather
--   than pooling seats. Its created_by/updated_by briefly hold a unique per-row import
--   reference used only to join license_allocations further below, then get reset back
--   to 'csv-import' at the end of this migration.
-- * users.email is synthesized (firstname.lastname@ppspl.in) since the sheet's Login ID
--   values are per-software-account logins, not personal emails.

-- Entities
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

-- Clients
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

-- Software catalog
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

-- Users (real employees only; shared/placeholder/unassigned computers are not users)
-- Hardware assets (one per distinct computer name; shared/placeholder and unassigned
-- spare computers have NULL assigned_user_id)
-- License inventory: one row per software-allocation line item (total_seats=1), preserving
-- each line's own cost/expiry/entity/client context rather than pooling seats.

-- License allocations: link each license_inventory row (matched via its temporary import
-- reference) to the resolved user/asset for that software line.
